[StringTable.1]
According to aerial reconnaissance, a large group of armored vehicles is approaching
[StringTable.2]
Anti-tank guns have arrived
[NewSubmission.Objectives]
Break through the enemy's defensive positions. According to the air reconnaissance data on the right flank of your armored group, the redeployment of Soviet artillery has been noticed. Allocate units of panzergrenadiers to search for and destroy a possible ambush of enemy anti-tank guns.
[NewSubmission.Description]
Early on the morning of July 5, Operation Citadel began. The 2nd SS Panzer Corps was advancing on the southern face of the Kursk Bulge. On the first day of the battle, his opponents were the 52nd Guards and 375th Rifle Division. With the powerful support of artillery and aviation, the SS divisions gradually "gnawed through" the defense of the Soviet troops. The 52nd Guards Division had a particularly hard time. By 15.00, the armored group of the SS division "Das Reich" almost broke through the defense of the 52nd Guards Division. Soviet command launched a counterattack with the help of the 230th tank Regiment to eliminate the breakthrough.
But all attempts to stop the advance of the German forces were unsuccessful. Despite the persistent resistance of the Soviet troops, by the evening the first army defense line was broken through.
[NewSubmission.Success]
[NewSubmission.Failed]
